Title: Fix for frontend infinite reload loop after login

Summary
- Symptom: The app reloaded ~3–4 times per second at http://localhost:5174, with backend logs showing 401/“not authorized”.
- Root cause: A stale/invalid token persisted from a previous session combined with an axios interceptor that forced a hard navigation on 401 created a loop.
  - Zustand persisted isAuthenticated = true.
  - On render, components made an authenticated request.
  - Backend returned 401 (invalid/expired token or new SECRET_KEY).
  - Interceptor cleared token and executed window.location.href = '/';
  - The app rehydrated immediately back to an authenticated state and repeated the cycle.

Changes Implemented
1) Avoid hard reload on 401 in axios interceptor
   - File: frontend/src/utils/api.ts
   - Change: On 401, clear localStorage token and call a store logout helper instead of window.location.href.
   - Result: No forced page refresh; the app drops to LoginPage cleanly.

2) Add a global logout helper (callable from anywhere)
   - File: frontend/src/services/store.ts
   - Added export: authLogout() that calls useAuthStore.getState().logout() safely.
   - Purpose: Allows the interceptor to reset auth state without navigating.

3) Add startup token validation guard
   - File: frontend/src/App.tsx
   - Added authChecked state and a useEffect that runs on mount:
     - If isAuthenticated but no auth_token in localStorage: logout.
     - If token exists: call /api/v1/auth/me once; on failure: logout.
     - Show a minimal "Loading..." splash until check completes.
   - Result: The app never renders protected sections with a bad token; it either stays logged in or lands on LoginPage—no loops.

Behavior After Fix
- If the stored token is valid: the app loads normally without looping.
- If the stored token is invalid/expired (e.g., SECRET_KEY changed): the app logs out once and shows the LoginPage, with no reload loop.
- Any in-session 401 now logs out without reloading the page.

Why This Works
- Removing window.location.href avoids hard reloads that could repeatedly rehydrate an invalid authenticated state.
- The bootstrap validator ensures the UI doesn’t make authenticated calls until the token is verified once.

How to Run
- Start (attached): docker compose up --build
- Start (detached): docker compose up --build -d
- Stop (attached): Ctrl+C
- If ports or containers get stuck: docker compose down && docker compose up --build

Notes & Recommendations
- Keeping backend SECRET_KEY stable preserves token validity across restarts. Even if it changes, the app will no longer loop; it will simply prompt for login again.
- Ensure backend CORS_ORIGINS includes http://localhost:5174 when using that port mapping.
- Consider implementing token refresh logic (using /api/v1/auth/refresh) if needed; the current setup logs out on 401 rather than attempting refresh.

Files Modified (relative to project root)
- frontend/src/services/store.ts (added authLogout helper)
- frontend/src/utils/api.ts (interceptor: remove hard reload, call authLogout)
- frontend/src/App.tsx (startup auth validation + loading gate)

